'''Blapsidæ''' (blap′si-dē), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Blaps'' + ''-idæ''.] A family of atracheliate heteromerous beetles, generally merged in ''Tenebrionidæ'', comprising nocturnal black-beetles of moderate size, the wings of which are generally obsolete and the elytra fused together. {{smaller|They frequent damp places, and when seized discharge in self-defense a liquid of a peculiar and penetrating odor.}}

