'''blasphemer''' (blȧs-fē′mėr), ''n.'' [< ME. ''blasfemere'', < ''blasfemen'', blaspheme.] One who blasphemes; one who speaks of God or of religion in impious and irreverent terms.
{{smaller block|<poem>Must . . . each ''blasphemer'' quite escape the rod,
Because the insult’s not on man but God?</poem>{{right|''Pope'', Epil. to Satires, ii. 195.}}}}

'''blasphemeress''' (blȧs-fē′mėr-es), ''n.'' [< ''blasphemer'' + ''-ess.''] A female blasphemer. [Rare.]
{{smaller block|A diabolical ''blasphemeresse'' of God.{{right|''Hall'', Hen. VI., an. 9.}}}}
